<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Grown from the original 180x70dp (3x1 cells) to fit the mini
     contribution grid HabitWidgetProvider now renders below the header —
     that plain a card was too cramped to show it at a legible size.

     minHeight is tuned against the *classic* cell-count formula older/
     non-targetCellHeight-aware launchers (e.g. Pixel/Nexus launcher)
     still use: cells = ceil((minHeight + 2) / 74). Confirmed via a live
     `uiautomator dump`: widget_content (header+grid) measures ~146dp
     tall, but the previous minHeight="150dp" resolves to ceil(152/74)=3
     grid cells — a whole extra ~113dp row of reserved space nothing
     fills — for the sake of being 4dp over the ceil(148/74)=2 threshold.
     146dp sits right at that 2-cell boundary. targetCellWidth/Height are
     left as the "2 cells" signal for launchers that DO read them
     directly (Android 12+); this only fixes the ones that don't.

     resizeMode allows both axes again: HabitWidgetProvider's grid now
     grows its row count to fill however tall the widget actually is
     (see renderGridBitmap), so a taller placement fills with more rows
     instead of leaving dead space — no need to cap height to prevent
     that anymore.

     minHeight dropped further, now 75dp — below the header+padding+
     margin alone (~78dp), let alone a full 7-row grid (~146dp needed
     total). This number is only a hint for the launcher's default
     cell-count math (unchanged at 2 cells either way — see above) and
     the actual rendered content still needs ~146dp to show without the
     dynamic row count in HabitWidgetProvider shrinking below MIN_ROWS=7
     and letterboxing. If a launcher ever did grant something this
     short, the grid would end up squeezed rather than absent. -->

<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:minHeight="75dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/habit_widget"
    android:configure="com.zstreak.app.MainActivity"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
